1
00:00:07,485 --> 00:00:09,094
Where does a ground come from?

2
00:00:10,057 --> 00:00:12,232
Not from the appearances themselves.

3
00:00:12,312 --> 00:00:16,267
They are many, particular,
and bound up in relation.

4
00:00:16,347 --> 00:00:18,133
It comes from two steps.

5
00:00:18,954 --> 00:00:21,048
The first step is abstraction.

6
00:00:21,128 --> 00:00:24,286
A common feature is drawn
out from the particulars.

7
00:00:24,416 --> 00:00:29,051
Think of "chariot", the same
across many assemblies of parts.

8
00:00:29,131 --> 00:00:32,461
Or "presence", across many experiences.

9
00:00:32,541 --> 00:00:36,256
Language, memory and
ordinary life depend on it.

10
00:00:37,078 --> 00:00:41,890
The second step is reification:
treating an idea as a thing.

11
00:00:41,970 --> 00:00:45,640
The abstraction is taken
to exist in its own right.

12
00:00:45,720 --> 00:00:49,879
It now seems to stand beneath
the particulars, grounding them.

13
00:00:49,959 --> 00:00:54,190
Only this second step creates the
sense of something standing behind.

14
00:00:54,997 --> 00:01:00,270
Examined, that unity is not found
apart from the faces it was drawn from.

15
00:01:00,350 --> 00:01:05,437
The ground was never there. It was
produced by reifying a useful abstraction.

16
00:01:06,257 --> 00:01:10,158
Dharmakīrti's theory of apoha, exclusion,

17
00:01:10,238 --> 00:01:12,101
is a helpful companion here.

18
00:01:12,181 --> 00:01:17,440
On that account, a general idea is
understood by excluding what it is not.

19
00:01:17,520 --> 00:01:20,212
It does not point to
a real common essence.

20
00:01:20,292 --> 00:01:24,166
Madhyamaka, the Middle Way
school, presses further.

21
00:01:24,246 --> 00:01:27,834
A commonality taken as a
ground has become svabhāva:

22
00:01:27,914 --> 00:01:31,276
own nature, a being
that stands on its own.

23
00:01:32,085 --> 00:01:36,312
So svabhāva is not found in
the content of an experience.

24
00:01:36,392 --> 00:01:41,950
Redness, sound and the feeling of presence
can be exactly as vivid either way.

25
00:01:42,030 --> 00:01:46,054
In this book's reading,
svabhāva is a matter of stance:

26
00:01:46,134 --> 00:01:47,806
how the appearing is held.

27
00:01:47,886 --> 00:01:50,728
Is it held as existing from its own side,

28
00:01:50,808 --> 00:01:52,616
independent of conditions?

29
00:01:52,696 --> 00:01:56,398
Is it held as the foundation from
which other things get their being?

30
00:01:57,230 --> 00:01:59,745
The same red can be held in two ways.

31
00:01:59,825 --> 00:02:02,313
In one, it is taken as a ground.

32
00:02:02,393 --> 00:02:04,677
Everything else is measured against it.

33
00:02:04,757 --> 00:02:07,042
In the other, it simply appears.

34
00:02:07,122 --> 00:02:10,629
It relates to light, to
the eye, to attention,

35
00:02:10,709 --> 00:02:12,830
and nothing is placed beneath it.

36
00:02:12,910 --> 00:02:14,637
The first is svabhāva.

37
00:02:14,717 --> 00:02:19,134
The second is dependent origination:
arising through conditions.

38
00:02:19,214 --> 00:02:23,486
The red is the same. The difference
lies entirely in the stance.

39
00:02:24,293 --> 00:02:28,995
This is why the taste of presence cannot
be a foundation that analysis finally

40
00:02:29,075 --> 00:02:32,759
reaches. Seen without
anything standing behind it,

41
00:02:32,839 --> 00:02:35,694
appearance is dependent
through and through.

42
00:02:35,774 --> 00:02:38,737
Its immediacy is that
of something relating,

43
00:02:38,817 --> 00:02:40,807
not of something standing alone.

44
00:02:41,625 --> 00:02:44,511
It also explains why the
habit is hard to see.

45
00:02:44,614 --> 00:02:47,604
Through language, perception and emotion,

46
00:02:47,684 --> 00:02:52,007
the mind has learned to treat each
vivid appearance as a thing with a fixed

47
00:02:52,087 --> 00:02:57,768
character. The habit is so reliable that
the naming disappears into what is named.

48
00:02:57,848 --> 00:03:01,409
The sense of inherent
existence is not argued for.

49
00:03:01,489 --> 00:03:04,715
It is assumed, each time
an appearance is met.

50
00:03:05,533 --> 00:03:08,143
Repeated looking loosens the assumption.

51
00:03:08,223 --> 00:03:13,569
Each time the forming is watched, the
framework is seen to be added, not found.

52
00:03:14,369 --> 00:03:19,588
What was taken as a fact about the world
is recognised as a way of relating to it.

53
00:03:19,668 --> 00:03:23,736
A way that works, without needing
to be true from its own side.

